WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.377
No time for the full interview? Quick start takes about a minute.

00:00:04.377 --> 00:00:13.837
Tap the things that matter to you — here, short trips, layovers worth having, little standby, easy to commute, protect my sleep and fewer legs a day.

00:00:13.837 --> 00:00:20.820
Then put them in order: drag one above another, or use the arrows, so the one that matters most is at the top.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:26.407
Or start from a pilot like you. You can always sharpen it with the full interview later.

00:00:32.373 --> 00:00:36.869
Everything you've told Line Select is kept on your Preferences page.

00:00:36.869 --> 00:00:41.828
Each priority shows how much it counts and what you said that put it there.

00:00:41.828 --> 00:00:48.639
Make one count more or less, or take it off with "Doesn't matter", and your rankings update right away.

00:00:49.339 --> 00:00:52.157
Got a new commute, or a date you need off?

00:00:52.157 --> 00:00:58.464
Tell it in your own words under "Tell us something new", and it reads it into your priorities.

00:00:59.458 --> 00:01:02.365
When next month's pack comes out, load it.

00:01:02.365 --> 00:01:08.386
Your preferences carry forward, and a short check-in catches anything that's different.

